CORE
justice-multi.aag
--bound 10
^\[justice0\] : PROVED up to bound 10$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
AIGER regression for a justice set with more than one literal. The latch
"toggle" alternates between 0 and 1, so both literals of the justice set
{toggle, !toggle} hold infinitely often, but never simultaneously.

A justice set is a generalized Büchi condition and must be encoded as
GF(l1) & ... & GF(ln), not GF(l1 & ... & ln). The correct encoding
reports PROVED; the (previously buggy) simultaneous encoding would
compute GF(toggle & !toggle) = GF(false) and spuriously report REFUTED.
